  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> be a continuous function. Then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;is equal to:"
  },
